+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The app wants to show how old a task is and what changed recently, but tasks carry no time information.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- On `add` the two are equal.
+- Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging and untagging a task set its `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- The list takes its time from a clock supplied by the caller (default: the system clock, set up outside `src/domain/`), so the domain stays free of wall-clock reads.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-timestamps`: creation and last-change times recorded on every task.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts` (`Task` type and the functions that change a task), `src/domain/list.ts` (clock), `src/index.ts` (default clock, public API), `test/list.test.ts`.
+- `createTodoList` gains an optional clock parameter; existing callers keep working. Tasks gain two fields.
+- No new dependency.
